[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its own cause table
already disagrees. Read by what each report says, the reports merged into it are three problems
with three fixes. The queued parser fix closes only the first.

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser leaves the booking-v3 form and the one-day moves broken. Keep #4471 open
until each problem below has its own fix.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  issues={{ parser: `${ISSUES}/1`, hint: `${ISSUES}/2`, 'one-day': `${ISSUES}/3` }}
/>

**`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes
the day first. Day and month come out swapped: "Booked for 2 December. The invite says
12 February."

**`hint`**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month
first as told, and the form reads the date day first, the tenant's way. Same swap, different
bug: the fix is in the form, not the parser.

**`one-day`**: a booking moves by one day, or shows a different day in Lisbon and Toronto.
Nothing is swapped. That is a timezone or daylight-saving conversion. The desk spotted these
([desk notes](https://github.com/felixo-szdm/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/blob/main/src/lib/data/desk-notes.json))
and counts them under `parser` by tenant, so they sit in that row too; a parser fix will not close them.

## How they ended up in one ticket

- **Merging by subject** ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). All three
  problems produce the same subjects: "Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong". Matching
  subjects merged them without anyone reading a body.
- **Intake tags are a guess from the reporter's browser.** Every report tagged `hint` came from
  an en-US browser, whatever its tenant or form. The tag is no guide to the cause.
- **The export repeats rows.** Its pages overlap, so count by report id.

## For the desk

- Group by tenant, form and channel (`causes.ts`), not by subject.
- Read a sample of each group's bodies before you call a big ticket one issue.
- A decision record is never edited; a new one should replace 0001.

